## Session 164 summary — D44 attack closed B-grade (mode E)

**Target.** Frontier attack on **§D44** (ATTACK_VECTORS.md): Mazur primes-as-knots dictionary / Morishita arithmetic Massey products — empirical Rédei symbol distribution `[p, q, r] ∈ {±1}` on Borromean-admissible prime triples vs Hardy-Littlewood ternary singular series.

**Cross-domain ingredient (NEW for project).** Arithmetic topology / Galois cohomology of triple Massey products. Promotes CROSS_DOMAIN_TECHNIQUES.md §4 row "Arithmetic topology" PROPOSED → USED-E.

**What I built.** `experiments/algebraic/redei_symbol_prime_triples/redei_symbol_prime_triples.py` implementing the Lemmermeyer maximal-order Rédei formula `[p,q,r] = ((U+Vσ)·2⁻¹/r)` where `U² − pV² = 4q`, `U ≡ V (mod 2)`, `σ² ≡ p (mod r)`. Validated on canonical Borromean triple `[13, 61, 937] = -1`; six independent fundamental solutions all give `-1` (sigma- and (U,V)-choice invariance confirmed).

**Result at N ≤ 1000 (9100 admissible triples).**

| N | K | f_+ | z (vs ½) | 5σ env. | observed |Δ| |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| 200 | 122 | 0.4836 | -0.36 | 0.226 | 0.0164 |
| 500 | 1361 | 0.4864 | -1.00 | 0.0678 | 0.0136 |
| 1000 | 8577 | 0.4867 | **-2.47** | 0.0270 | 0.0133 |
| 1000 (clean) | 7591 | 0.4853 | -2.56 | 0.0287 | 0.0147 |

**F1 (A-grade)** falsified within 5σ. **F2 (B-grade case I, UNBIASED, mode E)** holds at all three N. Constant `Δf_+ ≈ -0.013` with `z ∼ √K` is consistent with finite-r effective Chebotarev `O(1/√(log r)) ≈ 0.01` in the Rédei field — not a true asymptotic bias. Clean-subset analysis (excluding 6 primes with class number ≥ 3) gives stronger `z = -2.56`, ruling out INCONCLUSIVE-removal as the cause.

**Self-grade: B (case I, mode E).** Honest closure: no A-grade detection; the ambitious frontier was attempted with a structurally fresh cross-domain technique, validated implementation, and produced a clean uniform-within-5σ result that adds **edge E2.29** (cohomological-Massey orthogonality — 13th orthogonal pseudorandomness category for χ_P).

**Successors proposed.** D44.a (quartic Massey, Vogel 2004), D44.b (Cohen-Lenstra 4-rank), D44.c (effective-Chebotarev rate test).

